This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Two of the rule's three shapes apply, either alone being sufficient.

Its SUBJECT is scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh (its --efficiency-only and --archive arms), which
is not installed: install.sh's copy loop derives from core/fixtures/ and core/scripts/, and never
touches the repo-root scripts/. On a consumer it would resolve no validator and could only refuse or
pass without having checked anything.

It is also a MUTATION BATTERY behind a distribution-only fixture: it sources
core/fixtures/backlog-receipt-binding/run.sh, itself .dist-only, for its harness, and every one of its
twenty-eight mutants edits a seeded copy of that validator. It holds the efficiency-close block that
BL-982 split out of backlog-receipt-binding, and carries that fixture's declaration for the same reason.
